(A Prospective Evaluation of Integrated Online Care Coordination for Managing Pruritis and) Tj
T*
(Sleep Disruption in Atopic Dermatitis: Study Design and Methods) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Atopic dermatitis remains a chronic inflammatory condition with significant morbidity,) Tj
T*
(particularly regarding itch severity and secondary sleep disturbance. Coordinated) Tj
T*
(multidisciplinary care delivery via digital platforms may offer improved accessibility and) Tj
T*
(outcomes. This randomized trial will enroll approximately 100 adult participants with) Tj
T*
(clinically confirmed atopic dermatitis from dermatology clinics. Participants will be) Tj
T*
(randomized 1:1 to receive either integrated online care coordination involving clinical) Tj
T*
(assessment, treatment optimization, and supportive messaging, or continued standard) Tj
T*
(routine care. The online platform will include specialist nurse support, treatment) Tj
T*
(adherence monitoring, and patient education modules. Primary outcome is objective and) Tj
T*
(subjective measures of pruritis intensity at 12 weeks. Secondary outcomes include) Tj
T*
(standardized sleep quality assessments, disease severity scoring, and dermatitis-specific) Tj
T*
(quality-of-life instruments. Baseline disease severity, comorbidities, and psychosocial) Tj
T*
(factors will be documented. Data collection will occur at baseline and 12 weeks post-) Tj
T*
(randomization. Analysis will employ mixed-model intent-to-treat methodology.) Tj
